---
import Base from "../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import ComponentPreview from "../../../components/ComponentPreview.astro";
import {
  checkboxGroupScript,
  checkboxGroupTree,
  checkboxTree,
  tileCheckboxTree,
} from "../../../demos/checkbox";
import { getLocale, useTranslations } from "../../../i18n";
import StylingHooks from "../../../components/StylingHooks.astro";

const t = useTranslations(getLocale(Astro.url));




const tileCheckboxVanilla = `import { initComponents } from "@skryensya/vanilla/auto";
import { mountIcons } from "@skryensya/vanilla/icon";
import { lucideIcons } from "@skryensya/icons-lucide";

// The check/remove indicators are authored as placeholders
// <span data-sk-icon>; mountIcons replaces them with the <svg> from the set.
mountIcons(document, lucideIcons);

// Each label is authored with data-sk-tile-checkbox (data-name, data-value,
// data-default-checked) plus its input and its indicator.
// initComponents hydrates them with the @zag-js/checkbox machine.
await initComponents();

for (const root of document.querySelectorAll(
  "[data-sk-tile-checkbox]",
)) {
  root.addEventListener("sk:checkedchange", (event) => {
    console.log(root.dataset.value, event.detail.checked);
  });
}`;

---

<Base title="Checkbox" description="Native checkbox: independent, indeterminate state and machine-less form.">
  <h1>Checkbox</h1>
  <p class="lede">An independent choice. Keep a <code>input type="checkbox"</code>: submit, reset, keyboard and validation belong to the browser.</p>

  <ComponentPreview tree={checkboxTree(t)} label="Checkbox" />
  <p>
    The control uses the <code>check</code> and <code>remove</code> icon set roles, not a CSS stroke. Imports <code>@skryensya/core/components/checkbox.css</code> and calls <code>initComponents()</code> once.
  </p>

  <h2>A checkbox that groups other</h2>
  <p>
    <code>indeterminate</code> is not a third value that someone can choose: it is what a parent says when <strong>their children cannot agree</strong>. That is why the glyph is <code>remove</code> and not a half-check, and that is why the parent does not send anything to the form, those with <code>name</code> and <code>value</code> are the children.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview
    tree={checkboxGroupTree(t)}
    js={checkboxGroupScript}
    previewScript={checkboxGroupScript}
    label="Select all"
    note="three states from two booleans"
  />
  <p>
    The state of the parent is <strong>derived from</strong>, never authored: it is recalculated from the children on each change. On the contrary, a father with his own status begins to lie as soon as someone marks a child. There are fifteen lines without a machine or a new component, so the system does not involve it: grouping is a rule of the form, not of the control.
  </p>

  <h2>Surface checkbox: TileCheckbox</h2>
  <p>
    When the choice needs title, description and the entire surface as a target, use <code>TileCheckbox</code>. It is the same control (<code>sk-checkbox__control</code> + icons); just change the container.
  </p>
  <ComponentPreview tree={tileCheckboxTree(t)} label="TileCheckbox" />
  <p>The <code>tile-checkbox</code> enhancer (Svelte + <code>@zag-js/checkbox</code>, same machine as React) hydrates each <code>data-sk-tile-checkbox</code> label with <code>initComponents()</code>: controls its <code>input[data-part="input"]</code> (hidden) and syncs <code>data-state</code>; the <code>[data-part="indicator"]</code> is the visual control.</p>
  <CodeBlock code={tileCheckboxVanilla} label="JavaScript" />

  <h2>React</h2>
  <p>The code is in the <strong>React</strong> tab of the preview. React draws the icons from the linked set.</p>

  <h2>Contract</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>defaultChecked</code> leaves the state to the input; a reset returns to that value.</li>
    <li><code>checked</code> controls the value; <code>onCheckedChange</code> communicates the intent.</li>
    <li><code>"indeterminate"</code> is visual: it does not send a value until the person chooses checked or unchecked. The glyph is <code>remove</code>.</li>
    <li>
      A parent that groups children <strong>derives</strong> its state from them, it never saves it: <code>checked</code> when they are all there, <code>indeterminate</code> when they do not match. They are both input-independent flags, so turn off <code>indeterminate</code> when exiting that state or the script gets stuck.
    </li>
    <li>The text lives inside the <code>label</code>; if there is no text, it provides <code>aria-label</code>.</li>
    <li>
      The state layer goes in <code>sk-checkbox__control</code>, not in the label: the selection is the control's fill, and the text does not inherit the on-accent color.
    </li>
    <li>TileCheckbox reuses <code>sk-checkbox__control</code> and the same flags; does not invent another glyph.</li>
  </ul>
  <StylingHooks groups={[{ file: "components/checkbox.css", probe: "sk-checkbox" }]} />
</Base>
